cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Replication package for 'Same Storm, Different Boats: Generative AI and the Age Gradient Within Firms'"
message: "If you use this package, please cite the paper and the package."
type: software
# The paper's four authors, in the paper's order. Only ORCID iDs verified against
# the ORCID registry are given.
authors:
  - family-names: Lodefalk
    given-names: Magnus
    affiliation: "Örebro University; Ratio Institute"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0149-9598"
  - family-names: Löthman
    given-names: Lydia
    affiliation: "Örebro University"
  - family-names: Koch
    given-names: Michael
    affiliation: "Aarhus University; Kiel Institute for the World Economy"
  - family-names: Engberg
    given-names: Erik
    affiliation: "Örebro University; Ratio Institute"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4622-6526"
abstract: >-
  Code, documentation and aggregated exports behind the paper's estimates: the
  download and processing of the public job advertisements and auxiliary data, the
  posting analyses, the register scripts run inside Statistics Sweden's MONA
  environment (project P1207) with the disclosure-reviewed aggregates they exported,
  the builders of every table and figure, and a verification suite that checks each
  printed number against its source.
keywords:
  - replication package
  - generative artificial intelligence
  - job postings
  - young workers
  - register data
# Code under MIT (LICENSE); documentation, exports and derived tables under
# CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-docs).
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Magnus-L/canaries-sweden"
version: "2026-09-26"
date-released: "2026-09-26"
# DOI PLACEHOLDER: the package will be deposited on Zenodo through a GitHub
# release on acceptance. Add the DOI it assigns here, as
#   doi: "10.5281/zenodo.<to be assigned on deposit>"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Same Storm, Different Boats: Generative AI and the Age Gradient Within Firms"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lodefalk
        given-names: Magnus
      - family-names: Löthman
        given-names: Lydia
      - family-names: Koch
        given-names: Michael
      - family-names: Engberg
        given-names: Erik
    year: 2026
    notes: "Revised version submitted to Economics Letters (EL67898R1), October 2026 [date to be set at submission]; earlier version Örebro University Working Paper 2026:2 and Ratio Working Paper 388. Replaced with the journal reference at acceptance."
